Z||000010||Cliff Pennock||02-03-2001||08:46 PM||||Hugh, I couldn't agree <B>less</B>. Sure there are people on this world that could benefit more from these or any funds. But in the free world you have a choice whom or what to help. Last summer a firework-factory exploded downtown a major city here in the Netherlands. Hundreds of people lost their homes. All of them had jobs and would - in time - be able to get back on their feet without any outside help. Yet a fund was opened and millions and millions of dollars was raised to get these people back in the saddle again. Would those millions be better spent somewhere else? Sure. $30 dollars per patient helps cure lepracy in certain third-world countries. Does this mean we had no business raising money for those relatively wealthy people who lost their homes? Of course not. It's more than natural to help those that are in some way close to us - people that we can relate to. That doesn't make us heartless or hypocritical. It makes us human. If it makes you feel better, give $5 to the Anhony Barber fund and $20 to the Red Cross. It's your choice. Like I said, we live in a free world.||||reg||1
Z||000011||hugh||02-03-2001||09:07 PM||||Cliff,I do not believe that the criteria  for receiving or giving help should be based on what type of car you drive.I do not see how this group of people on the forum buying a car for someone that has had a serious accident will in any way make his life better or lessen his pain and discomfort.I'm sure his family is extremely happy he survived and greatly appreciates the show of support from the forum members that have responded as they have.I do not feel the same as these people.I applaud them for what they have done,but my priorities lie elseware.||||reg||1
Z||000012||BAM-BAM||02-03-2001||11:30 PM||||  The problems throughout the world are none of our buisiness. Hell, we as a country can't even take care of the homeless and indigent within our own borders. You want to talk priorities. Why is it that the people of this country give more donations to foreign cocerns than they do to the starving children in our own cities. The fact that Mr. Barber drove a Fiero Is a point of comonality with every individual on this Forum. If you can't see that then you are blind. When a group such as this has the opportunity to stand up and be noticed, when the rest of the world would rather we just go away, I say we take the opportunity. Also, what is the comment about profitting? Who stands to proffit from any of this. This has been a nonproffit concern from the begining. That comment was just plain moronic. I personaly give thousands of dollars a year to charities that help the poor children of "THIS" country to eat, and to battered women and children to keep them safe. If you feel that your money is best kept in your bank and that $5.00 is to much to give to a fellow Fieroan who has fallen on hard times, then keep it there. But why try and stamp out any good that is being done? That "IS" plain selfish. Hell, I drop $5.00 in change in a month or spend twice that on nonsense. I don't see you point. We asked if people would help, many people responded with positive feedback. Yet those numbers are no reflective in the account numbers. Maybe those numbers will grow, maybe they won't. This is truly a sad day on the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I will have to rethink my faith here. <P> Bye, B2 OUT! <P> P. S. Maybe we should stop sharing our information when that information would be better kept to ourselves.||||reg||9
