4.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!!!"</B>||||reg||14
Z||000015||FieroMaster88||02-04-2001||02:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BAM-BAM:<BR><B>  That's a sad thing. I really thought we here on the forum could make a difference. I guess that most of us are to caught up in our lives to care about anyone else. That's the new world society, everyone for themselves and screw the rest. TO those who have shown the generosity to help Anthony, my hat is off to you. To those who felt that he wasn't deserving of mere pocket change, GOD help you in your time of need. <P> BYE, B2 OUT!<P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya know, I am not here to argue, but sometimes I get upset.  I am not trying to give a sob story either, but I go to college full time and have a part time job on the side.  I work maybe 17 hours a week. I have a car payment, insurance payment, gas and now that I am finally catching up with bills my damn tranny breaks and is going to cost me all of my extra money.  Dont get me wrong, I DO want to donate money, but sometimes people have other things to take care of before they can.....i guess i am trying to say just lighten up a little bit.  Give it time, the money will come.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||9
Z||000016||hugh||02-04-2001||08:59 AM||||I will address what I believe was directed at me. <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BAM-BAM:<BR><B>  The problems throughout the world are none of our buisiness. Hell, we as a country can't even take care of the homeless and indigent within our own borders. You want to talk priorities. Why is it that the people of this country give more donations to foreign cocerns than they do to the starving children in our own cities. The fact that Mr. Barber drove a Fiero Is a point of comonality with every individual on this Forum. If you can't see that then you are blind. When a group such as this has the opportunity to stand up and be noticed, when the rest of the world would rather we just go away, I say we take the opportunity. Also, what is the comment about profitting? Who stands to proffit from any of this. This has been a nonproffit concern from the begining. That comment was just plain moronic. I personaly give thousands of dollars a year to charities that help the poor children of "THIS" country to eat, and to battered women and children to keep them safe. If you feel that your money is best kept in your bank and that $5.00 is to much to give to a fellow Fieroan who has fallen on hard times, then keep it there. But why try and stamp out any good that is being done? That "IS" plain selfish. Hell, I drop $5.00 in change in a month or spend twice that on nonsense. I don't see you point. We asked if people would help, many people responded with positive feedback. Yet those numbers are no reflective in the account numbers. Maybe those numbers will grow, maybe they won't. This is truly a sad day on the Forum   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I will have to rethink my faith here. <P> Bye, B2 OUT! <P> P. S. Maybe we should stop sharing our information when that information would be better kept to ourselves.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>1st  Priorities are exactly what I am talking about,not sending anything to another country,or for that matter to another part of this country when there are so many things that can be done locally.Where I would have an exception to that feeling is when it would involve someone on this forum that I have a relationship with,and know or consider a friend.<BR>2nd<BR>  A point of commonality could also be with all the people on this forum who do the same kind of work,like the same sports,etc.How in the world does this form a criteria for what you suggest?<BR>3rd The rest of the world wants us to go away?I won't even comment on that statement.<BR>4th Reread my post,I never said anything that could be interpreted as being against other people giving to that fund.As I said before I applaud them for what they are doing,but my priorities lie elsewhere.<BR>5th The profit comment was not my post!<BR>6th<BR>   I think what some members are trying to do is commendable,but I don't like the way I or any other members are pictured as cheap or unfeeling because we don't agree with what you are doing.||||reg||1
Z||000017||stimpy||02-04-2001||09:36 AM||||Every once in a while, a huge groundswell of support for <B>something</B> spreads through the forum. Stickers, worldwide forum meet, now this. I don't want to sound apathetic, as I feel that these things are great in theory.  But truth be told, people would rather look across the street then in their own backyard. <P>When was the last time you saw on the news of the young couple expecting, burned out of their apartment with only the clothes on their back. What did you do then? When was the last time you donated blood? How anout something as simple as taking your car to the church parking lot carwash in stead of doing it yourself.<BR>There are always opportuniyies to give quietly.  I think many people took advantage of the unfortnate situation with Anthony to puff out their chest proudly and say "WE should do this." without making the personal commitment to follow through. I don't direct this at people who have really shown action, like Mr. Wayne Kayl, or people who have reached down to give, or even people who believe charity begins at home like hugh.<BR>No, I am talking to those 30-40 people who posted on the various Mr. Barber threads who stated that some relief should be provided. And have done nothing since. And while I point my finger, three more point back at me. Check goes out tomorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000018||BAM-BAM||02-04-2001||11:14 AM||||  Thank you Stimpy! That was a great statement. You see, that's the kind of person I am. I obviously can't donate to every cause, but I do my best to help where I can. Just yesterday I donated $5.00 to a local KEY Club at a free car wash, didn't even get my car washed. I have donated clothing to help people who were the victims of fire and flood here in Southern Nevada, I give to United way, I used to donate blood till two years ago when I contracted Hepatitus, I give to the Salvation Army whenever I have something that has outgrown it usefulness to me. I'm not puffing out my chest nor do I expect everyone to be like me. I give of my own free will with the knowledge of what it's like to be down with no help in site. I know what an impact a guesture like this would make in Anthony's life. Human kindness and compasion is some of the best medicine known to man. Not everybody has to donate to the ABF. But like Stimpy said, there was a great show of support in the begining and this is more directed towards those people, not the hugh's or Black88GT's. If you don't want to donate, then don't. But while to say you applaude those who have rallied you also condem the act by you negative, guilt ridden posts. You guys are obviously free to do what you want. But your words are a bit of a condemnation of this effort. Also, no one said the hugh made the comment about this being a for proffit concern. I believe it was Black88GT, for what ever reason.<P> Later, B2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000019||Jaygee79||02-04-2001||11:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>its really sad when people try to profit from somebody elses tradgedy...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I couldn't agree more.<P>Why I think everyone is upset about no donations coming in is because there were many people that agreed to help out if anything was done.  Now that something is being done, most of those people haven't done anything.  But like a previous poster said, it hasn't even been a full month yet.  Give it some more time.  And I also agree that some people have other priorities that need to be taken care of first.  It's great to help out others, but some things have to be taken care of first, like paying the rent, putting food on the table, making sure the car is ok for driving to and from work, etc.  Some people just aren't in the position right now to do anything yet.  And don't forget, tax time is fast approaching.  A lot of people are really strapped at this time of year until they get their refunds in.||||reg||1
Z||000020||fieroparts.com||02-04-2001||11:35 AM||||I hope you are NOT talking about me!<P>"its really sad when people try to profit from somebody elses tradgedy"<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Couldn't have said it better myself Hugh, you left out one thing though, its really sad when people try to profit from somebody elses tradgedy...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||BAM-BAM||02-04-2001||01:09 PM||||  I believe they are Tim. Let me take a minute to explain this if I may. Tim  contacted me and others to discussed his idea on how to raise funds for Anthony Barber. We all thought it was a good idea providing that there wasn't a preception of proffitability. There isn't a chance in hell for Tim to proffit from this. At best it will be a break even deal with any and all proffit going to the ABF. Tim has three or four T-Top sets on his shelves and they take up alot of room. These tops are no longer made and keeping them on hand prevents Tim from stocking more readily available items on those shelves. His idea for just gettin rid of one to make room was to raffle it off with the profits going to ABF. How much better would this have been received if tim just offered the raffle without ABF being mentioned. I think that a shot at a $3000.00 T-Top set would be well worth the $50.00 and few questions would be asked and fewer fingers pointed. Rest assured there is no profit being made here and the proffit that is made goes directly to ABF. Please relinquish the implications. It's not neccessary.<P> Thanks, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000022||hugh||02-04-2001||03:30 PM||||<BR>Bam-Bam'What the hell is your problem?Where do you get guilt ridden posts or condemnation by me?It is obvious to me that no matter what I may say unless I agree with you I am wrong.This is the last post I intend to make on this subject.I think what is being done for Anthony is commendable and anyone who would say otherwise is not being honest with themselves,butAGAIN,I do not wish to nor will be coerced into doing something I do not believe in.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||BAM-BAM||02-04-2001||05:03 PM||||  Well hugh, How about the fact that no one has attempted to coerce you into anything and  the fact that you responded to the original post as though it was you that was the subject. I could care less what reason you have for not wanting to donate to this or any other cause. But, when you come off as though you are being chastised for not contributing when you were not even mentioned, it's seems defensive and as a result you are greeted with counter defense. I and others understand that not eveyone has the resources to donate, you all are not the subject. The subject is merely a reminder to those who jumped on the band wagon, that we are still looking for there support. If you cant' or won't contribute, that's fine. But the minute you voice your reasons and acuse me and others of coercion or trying to proffit, what do you expect. This is really getting out of hand as do flame wars where someone jumps in on something that they neither know anything about or is any of there buisness. I will not post to this thread again, it's just causing hard feelings. <P> Bye, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||8
